PyMieScatt 1.8.1.1 (PyPI sdist PyMieScatt-1.8.1.1.tar.gz) imports trapz from scipy.integrate,
which SciPy 1.14 removed; both certification references hold a newer SciPy. These two
lines take it from NumPy instead (numpy.trapezoid, NumPy 2.0 and later). Applied by
build_pymiescatt_standin.py, which requires each removed line at its stated line number
(no context, no fuzz). The sdist's sources end their lines in CRLF; each line written
takes the ending of the line it replaces.

--- a/PyMieScatt/Inverse.py
+++ b/PyMieScatt/Inverse.py
@@ -9 +9 @@
-from scipy.integrate import trapz
+from numpy import trapezoid as trapz
--- a/PyMieScatt/Mie.py
+++ b/PyMieScatt/Mie.py
@@ -5 +5 @@
-from scipy.integrate import trapz
+from numpy import trapezoid as trapz
